# Development Workflow

Local commands mirror CI pipeline. Always run `make check` before pushing.

## Quick Reference

```bash
make check    # Run before pushing (lint + type-check + test)
make ci       # Full CI simulation including build
make dev      # Start dev server
```

## CI Pipeline Stages

CI runs these stages in order. PRs to `main` must pass all stages.

| Stage | Local Command | CI Job |
|-------|--------------|--------|
| Lint | `make lint` or `npm run lint` | `lint` |
| Type Check | `make type-check` or `npm run type-check` | `type-check` |
| Test | `make test` or `npm run test:run` | `test` |
| Build | `make build` or `npm run build` | `build` |

## Pre-Push Checklist

1. `make check` passes
2. No TypeScript errors (`npm run type-check`)
3. Tests pass (`npm run test:run`)
4. Lint clean (`npm run lint`)

## Branch Strategy

- `dev` — Active development
- `main` — Production-ready code (protected, requires CI pass)
- Feature branches → PR to `dev` → PR to `main`

## Common Workflows

### Adding a feature
```bash
git checkout -b feature/name
# ... make changes ...
make check           # Verify locally
git add . && git commit -m "feat: description"
git push -u origin HEAD
# Create PR to dev
```

### Fixing lint/type errors
```bash
make lint            # See lint errors
make type-check      # See type errors
# Fix issues, then verify
make check
```

### Running tests during development
```bash
make test-watch      # Interactive watch mode
make test            # Single run
make test-coverage   # With coverage report
```
